<section class="nu-section nu-fit" aria-labelledby="nulang-fit-heading">
  <div class="nu-container">
    <div class="nu-section-header">
      <h2 id="nulang-fit-heading">Is Nulang right for your project?</h2>
      <p class="nu-section-subhead">Nulang is an alpha language for exploring typed actors, supervised failures, and opt-in durable state. Its design is promising, but its ecosystem and operational maturity are still developing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fit-grid">
      <div class="fit-card">
        <h3>Good reasons to experiment</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Prototype concurrent services with actor isolation and supervision.</li>
          <li>Explore static types, row-polymorphic effects, and reference capabilities in one language.</li>
          <li>Evaluate persistent actors and restart recovery using your own failure tests.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="fit-card fit-caution">
        <h3>Choose a mature stack when</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>You need production SLAs, established tooling, or a large package ecosystem today.</li>
          <li>You need proven multi-node failover: clustering and distribution remain experimental.</li>
          <li>You are building a conventional web frontend or a simple CLI application.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
